        <ArticleTitle>Caffeine ingestion and 5-km running time trial performance</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>Twelve trained runners ingested 3 mg/kg caffeine or placebo 60 minutes before a 5-km time trial in a double-blind crossover design. Caffeine improved finishing time by 1.1 percent relative to placebo, and ratings of perceived exertion were unchanged between conditions despite the faster pace.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
